Track 2: Why Keep the Demagnetizer Dry?
- Story & Context: Tied to the rusty fuel dock at Eomgung Sluice, junior deckhand Min-seo scrubbed salt grime from his cassette demagnetizing wand using a rag soaked in kerosene, terrified his grandmother would throw his synth pedals into the river for interrupting the dawn market's rhythm. He confessed through the barge's cabin window that he had deliberately dubbed bedroom jangle pop over her beloved morning raga tapes because he was too shy to speak to the girl who ran the persimmon sampan across the slip. Hearing the stammering, syncopated claps echoing from his deck, his grandmother stepped out, patted his shoulder with flour-covered hands, and whispered, "Tell me which orbit you were trying to hide in that magnetic dust."
