Track 3: Unspooled Ferrite Braids the Current
- Story & Context: When the city government finally severed the moorings of the floating produce market to make way for a concrete marina, the elder matriarchs ceremonially emptied twenty crates of tangled magnetic cassettes into the tidal wash. Divers maintaining the canal gates months later claimed the brown ribbons had wound themselves into the mangrove roots, supposedly emitting a steady drone that tuned the morning tide to a slow seven-beat slap against the hulls. Young buskers still gather on the concrete embankments to clap in time with the water's suction, honoring the legend of Sun-hee's final pre-dawn broadcast: "Throw the broken play-heads to the tide and let the sky tune your string."
